ALL.append(q(482,"Hard","CSE-style: What is the function of 'the employees having been notified' in: 'The employees having been notified, the meeting proceeded as scheduled'?",["Subject of main clause","Direct object","Absolute phrase (modifies main clause)","Participial phrase (modifies 'meeting')"],"Absolute phrase (modifies main clause)","It has its own subject ('employees') and modifies the entire main clause — classic absolute phrase.",["absolute phrase","function","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(483,"Hard","CSE-style: Which analysis is correct for: 'The manager told the staff that the deadline had been moved to Friday'?",["'the staff' = IO; 'that the deadline had been moved to Friday' = DO","'the staff' = DO; 'that the deadline had been moved to Friday' = object complement","'the staff' = DO; 'that the deadline had been moved to Friday' = adverb","'the staff' = IO; 'that the deadline had been moved to Friday' = subject complement"],"'the staff' = DO; 'that the deadline had been moved to Friday' = object complement","With 'told,' the person told is the DO. The 'that' clause tells what was told — it complements the DO.",["direct object","object complement","told"]))
ALL.append(q(484,"Hard","CSE-style: Which analysis is correct for: 'She gave the committee her resignation letter'?",["'the committee' = DO; 'her resignation letter' = OC","'the committee' = IO; 'her resignation letter' = DO","'the committee' = subject complement; 'her resignation letter' = DO","'the committee' = DO; 'her resignation letter' = IO"],"'the committee' = IO; 'her resignation letter' = DO","Gave what? → her resignation letter (DO). Gave to whom? → the committee (IO, between verb and DO).",["indirect object","direct object","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(485,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The policy, controversial as it may be, has been implemented nationwide,' what is 'controversial as it may be'?",["Adjective clause","Adverb clause (concession)","Parenthetical concessive phrase","Subject complement"],"Parenthetical concessive phrase","It's a concessive parenthetical (= although it may be controversial), set off by commas.",["concessive","parenthetical","structure"]))
ALL.append(q(486,"Hard","CSE-style: Identify the sentence with NO structural error.",["The committee, after careful deliberation, and considering all the evidence presented.","Having reviewed the documents, it was decided that the complaint should be dismissed.","The director, whose leadership has been widely praised, announced her retirement effective next month.","The report submitted by the team, which was comprehensive, however, it contained minor errors."],"The director, whose leadership has been widely praised, announced her retirement effective next month.","Clear structure: subject + relative clause + verb + DO. Others have fragments, dangling modifiers, or run-ons.",["correct structure","CSE-style","elimination"]))
ALL.append(q(487,"Hard","CSE-style: What structural error does this contain? 'Having reviewed all the evidence, it was decided that the complaint should be dismissed.'",["Comma splice","Run-on sentence","Dangling modifier","Fragment"],"Dangling modifier","'Having reviewed all the evidence' implies a person reviewed, but the subject is 'it' (expletive). The modifier dangles.",["dangling modifier","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(488,"Hard","CSE-style: What structural error does this contain? 'The committee approved the budget, they also allocated funds for training.'",["Fragment","Dangling modifier","Comma splice","Misplaced modifier"],"Comma splice","Two independent clauses joined by only a comma.",["comma splice","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(489,"Hard","CSE-style: What structural error does this contain? 'The proposal submitted by the department head after consulting with all division chiefs and reviewing the budget allocation for the current fiscal year.'",["Comma splice","Run-on sentence","Dangling modifier","Fragment (no main verb)"],"Fragment (no main verb)","'Submitted' and 'consulting' and 'reviewing' are all participles/gerunds — no finite verb serves as the predicate.",["fragment","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(490,"Hard","CSE-style: What structural error does this contain? 'Although the investigation revealed serious irregularities in the procurement process and the committee recommended immediate action.'",["Comma splice","Run-on sentence","Fragment (dependent clause only)","Misplaced modifier"],"Fragment (dependent clause only)","'Although' makes the entire structure a dependent clause — there's no independent clause to complete the thought.",["fragment","dependent clause","CSE-style"]))

# --- Advanced Sentence Analysis (Hard 491-540) ---
ALL.append(q(491,"Hard","In 'It was the director who approved the controversial policy,' what type of structure is this?",["Simple sentence","Cleft sentence (emphasis structure)","Compound sentence","Fragment"],"Cleft sentence (emphasis structure)","'It was...who...' is a cleft construction that emphasizes 'the director.'",["cleft sentence","emphasis","structure"]))
ALL.append(q(492,"Hard","In 'What surprised everyone was that the committee reversed its decision,' identify the subject and subject complement.",["Subject: 'What surprised everyone'; Complement: 'that the committee reversed its decision'","Subject: 'everyone'; Complement: 'the committee'","Subject: 'What'; Complement: 'decision'","Subject: 'that the committee reversed its decision'; Complement: 'What surprised everyone'"],"Subject: 'What surprised everyone'; Complement: 'that the committee reversed its decision'","Noun clause subject + linking verb 'was' + noun clause complement.",["noun clause","subject","complement","analysis"]))
ALL.append(q(493,"Hard","In 'The more carefully you analyze the sentence, the easier it becomes to identify its components,' how many clauses are there?",["One","Two","Three","Four"],"Three","(1) The more carefully you analyze the sentence (2) the easier it becomes (3) to identify its components (infinitive clause as subject of 'becomes' — debatable, but the correlative has two main clauses + the infinitive).",["clause count","correlative comparative"]))
ALL.append(q(494,"Hard","What is the function of 'there' in: 'There seems to be a discrepancy in the financial records'?",["Adverb of place","Expletive/dummy subject","Direct object","Subject complement"],"Expletive/dummy subject","'There' is a placeholder. The logical subject is 'a discrepancy.'",["expletive","there","function"]))
ALL.append(q(495,"Hard","In 'The committee recommended the proposal be adopted immediately,' what is unusual about the verb 'be'?",["It is in passive voice.","It is a linking verb.","It is in the subjunctive mood (base form after 'recommended that').","It is an infinitive."],"It is in the subjunctive mood (base form after 'recommended that').","After verbs of recommendation + (that), the subjunctive base form is used: 'be' instead of 'is/was.'",["subjunctive","mandative","grammar"]))
ALL.append(q(496,"Hard","In 'She is the kind of leader whom people willingly follow,' what is the function of 'whom'?",["Subject of 'follow'","Direct object of 'follow'","Object of preposition","Subject complement"],"Direct object of 'follow'","People follow whom? → whom (= the leader). 'Whom' is the DO inside the relative clause.",["relative pronoun","whom","function"]))
ALL.append(q(497,"Hard","In 'The report, the findings of which contradicted earlier studies, was published last month,' what is the function of 'which'?",["Subject of 'contradicted'","Direct object of 'contradicted'","Object of preposition 'of'","Subject complement"],"Object of preposition 'of'","'Of which' = 'of the report.' 'Which' is the object of 'of.' The subject of 'contradicted' is 'findings.'",["relative pronoun","object of preposition","complex"]))
ALL.append(q(498,"Hard","In 'Seldom has the government implemented a policy so swiftly,' why is the word order inverted?",["It is a question.","The sentence begins with a negative/restrictive adverb.","It is in passive voice.","It contains a relative clause."],"The sentence begins with a negative/restrictive adverb.","Fronting negative adverbs (seldom, rarely, never, hardly) triggers subject-auxiliary inversion.",["inversion","negative adverb","structure"]))
ALL.append(q(499,"Hard","In 'Were the committee to approve the proposal, implementation would begin immediately,' what structure is used?",["Past tense conditional","Subjunctive inversion (formal conditional without 'if')","Question form","Imperative"],"Subjunctive inversion (formal conditional without 'if')","'Were...to approve' = 'If the committee were to approve.' Formal English inverts subject and 'were' to replace 'if.'",["subjunctive inversion","conditional","formal"]))
ALL.append(q(500,"Hard","In 'The director insisted on the employees' submitting their reports on time,' what is 'the employees' submitting their reports on time'?",["Direct object of 'insisted'","Object of preposition 'on'","Subject complement","Appositive"],"Object of preposition 'on'","'On' is the preposition; the gerund phrase 'the employees' submitting their reports on time' is its object.",["gerund phrase","object of preposition","possessive with gerund"]))

ALL.append(q(501,"Hard","CSE-style: Which sentence correctly uses a nonrestrictive clause?",["The employees who completed the training received certificates.","The employees, who completed the training, received certificates.","The employees, who completed the training received certificates.","The employees who completed the training, received certificates."],"The employees, who completed the training, received certificates.","Nonrestrictive clauses are set off by commas on BOTH sides. This implies ALL employees completed training.",["nonrestrictive clause","punctuation","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(502,"Hard","CSE-style: What is the difference in meaning between 'The employees who completed the training received certificates' and 'The employees, who completed the training, received certificates'?",["No difference.","First: only some employees (those who completed) got certificates. Second: all employees completed and all got certificates.","First: all employees. Second: only some employees.","First is incorrect; second is correct."],"First: only some employees (those who completed) got certificates. Second: all employees completed and all got certificates.","Restrictive (no commas) limits which employees. Nonrestrictive (commas) adds info about all employees.",["restrictive vs nonrestrictive","meaning","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(503,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The fact remains that the funds were misused,' what is the function of 'that the funds were misused'?",["Subject","Direct object of 'remains'","Subject complement (predicate nominative)","Noun clause in apposition to 'fact'"],"Noun clause in apposition to 'fact'","The clause explains what the fact is — it's in apposition to 'fact.' 'Remains' is intransitive here.",["noun clause","appositive","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(504,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'She is not what she used to be,' what is the function of 'what she used to be'?",["Subject","Direct object","Subject complement","Adverb"],"Subject complement","After the linking verb 'is,' the noun clause describes/renames 'She.'",["noun clause","subject complement","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(505,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'I will support whatever decision the committee makes,' what is the function of 'whatever decision the committee makes'?",["Subject","Direct object","Object of preposition","Subject complement"],"Direct object","Will support what? → whatever decision the committee makes (noun clause as DO).",["noun clause","direct object","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(506,"Hard","CSE-style: Analyze the sentence: 'The policy that the director implemented, which many employees opposed, has nonetheless improved productivity.' How many dependent clauses are there?",["One","Two","Three","Four"],"Two","(1) 'that the director implemented' (restrictive relative, modifies 'policy') (2) 'which many employees opposed' (nonrestrictive relative, modifies 'policy').",["clause count","relative clauses","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(507,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'Had the committee been informed earlier, the problem could have been prevented,' what is the subject of the main clause?",["committee","problem","Had","prevented"],"problem","The main clause is 'the problem could have been prevented.' Subject: problem.",["subject","conditional inversion","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(508,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'Had the committee been informed earlier, the problem could have been prevented,' what is the subject of the conditional clause?",["committee","problem","Had","informed"],"committee","The conditional clause is 'Had the committee been informed earlier.' Subject: committee.",["subject","conditional inversion","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(509,"Hard","CSE-style: What is the function of 'for the project to succeed' in: 'It is essential for the project to succeed'?",["Subject","Direct object","Delayed subject (logical subject)","Adverb of purpose"],"Delayed subject (logical subject)","'It' is the dummy subject. The infinitive phrase 'for the project to succeed' is the logical subject.",["infinitive phrase","delayed subject","expletive"]))
ALL.append(q(510,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The longer the investigation takes, the more frustrated the public becomes,' identify the sentence structure.",["Simple sentence","Compound sentence","Correlative comparative (the...the...)","Complex sentence with adverb clause"],"Correlative comparative (the...the...)","This is a correlative comparative structure where two clauses are linked by 'the...the...'",["correlative comparative","structure","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(511,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'She not only passed the exam but also topped it,' what is the compound element?",["Compound subject","Compound predicate","Compound direct object","Compound sentence"],"Compound predicate","'Not only passed the exam but also topped it' — two verb phrases sharing the subject 'She.'",["compound predicate","correlative","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(512,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The committee will review the proposal and, if necessary, request additional documentation,' what is the compound element?",["Compound subject","Compound predicate","Compound direct object","Compound sentence"],"Compound predicate","Two verb phrases: 'will review the proposal' and '(will) request additional documentation.'",["compound predicate","parenthetical","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(513,"Hard","CSE-style: What is the function of 'as it may seem' in: 'Strange as it may seem, the policy has been effective'?",["Subject","Adverb clause (concession)","Adjective clause","Subject complement"],"Adverb clause (concession)","'Strange as it may seem' = 'Although it may seem strange.' It's a concessive adverbial clause.",["concessive clause","inversion","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(514,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The report is to be submitted by Friday,' what is the function of 'to be submitted by Friday'?",["Subject","Direct object","Subject complement (predicate phrase)","Adverb"],"Subject complement (predicate phrase)","After the linking verb 'is,' the infinitive phrase tells what the report is (scheduled to be). It completes the subject.",["infinitive","subject complement","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(515,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'All things considered, the project was a success,' what is 'All things considered'?",["Participial phrase modifying 'project'","Absolute phrase","Subject","Adverb clause"],"Absolute phrase","It has its own subject ('things') and participle ('considered'). It modifies the entire main clause.",["absolute phrase","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(516,"Hard","CSE-style: Which sentence uses 'that' as a relative pronoun (not a conjunction)?",["She said that she would attend.","The book that I borrowed is overdue.","It is important that everyone participate.","The fact that he resigned surprised us."],"The book that I borrowed is overdue.","In 'that I borrowed,' 'that' replaces 'the book' as the DO of 'borrowed' — it's a relative pronoun.",["that","relative pronoun vs conjunction","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(517,"Hard","CSE-style: Which sentence uses 'that' as a subordinating conjunction (not a relative pronoun)?",["The policy that was implemented has been effective.","The employee that submitted the report was commended.","She announced that the meeting was cancelled.","The building that collapsed was old."],"She announced that the meeting was cancelled.","'That' introduces a noun clause (DO of 'announced'). It has no grammatical role inside the clause — it's a conjunction.",["that","conjunction vs relative pronoun","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(518,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The committee, none of whose members had prior experience, was tasked with the investigation,' what is the function of 'whose'?",["Subject of the relative clause","Direct object","Possessive determiner modifying 'members'","Object of preposition"],"Possessive determiner modifying 'members'","'Whose' shows possession — it modifies 'members' (the committee's members).",["relative pronoun","whose","possessive"]))
ALL.append(q(519,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'She works harder than anyone else does,' what is the function of 'than anyone else does'?",["Adjective clause","Adverb clause (comparison)","Noun clause","Prepositional phrase"],"Adverb clause (comparison)","'Than' introduces a comparative clause modifying 'harder.'",["comparative clause","adverb","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(520,"Hard","CSE-style: In 'The question of whether to proceed remains unresolved,' what is the function of 'whether to proceed'?",["Subject","Direct object","Object of preposition 'of'","Subject complement"],"Object of preposition 'of'","'Whether to proceed' is a noun phrase (infinitive) serving as the object of the preposition 'of.'",["infinitive","object of preposition","CSE-style"]))

# --- Advanced Error Recognition and Correction (Hard 521-560) ---
ALL.append(q(521,"Hard","CSE-style: Which sentence is structurally correct?",["The committee, after reviewing the evidence and consulting with legal experts, has decided to proceed with the investigation.","The committee after reviewing the evidence and consulting with legal experts has decided to proceed with the investigation.","The committee, after reviewing the evidence and consulting with legal experts has decided to proceed with the investigation.","The committee after reviewing the evidence, and consulting with legal experts, has decided to proceed with the investigation."],"The committee, after reviewing the evidence and consulting with legal experts, has decided to proceed with the investigation.","Parenthetical phrase correctly set off by commas on BOTH sides.",["parenthetical","punctuation","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(522,"Hard","CSE-style: Which sentence is structurally correct?",["Not only did the policy reduce costs, but it also improved employee morale.","Not only the policy reduced costs, but it also improved employee morale.","Not only did the policy reduce costs but it also improved employee morale.","Not only did the policy reduced costs, but it also improved employee morale."],"Not only did the policy reduce costs, but it also improved employee morale.","'Not only' at the start triggers inversion (did + subject + base verb). Comma before 'but.'",["correlative conjunction","inversion","CSE-style"]))
ALL.append(q(523,"Hard","CSE-style: Which sentence has a dangling modifier?",["Concerned about the deadline, the manager extended the submission period.","Concerned about the deadline, the submission period was extended by the manager.","Because she was concerned about the deadline, the manager extended the submission period.","The manager, concerned about the deadline, extended the submission period."],"Concerned about the deadline, the submission period was extended by the manager.","'Concerned about the deadline' should modify a person, but the subject is 'the submission period.'",["dangling modifier","CSE-style"]))
